{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02342",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.58,
      "end_seconds": 8.92,
      "duration_seconds": 8.34,
      "text": "doctor, the patient's with us now i did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.4,
      "end_seconds": 14.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "okay, thanks hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.35,
      "end_seconds": 23.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.88,
      "text": "yeah, it's a shaky feeling in my hands i don't know what's causing it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.15,
      "end_seconds": 29.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Okay, when was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.46,
      "end_seconds": 40.03,
      "duration_seconds": 9.57,
      "text": "I'm not sure when it began, to be honest. Some weeks ago, but I can't say how many."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.38,
      "end_seconds": 51.86,
      "duration_seconds": 10.48,
      "text": "right, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.06,
      "end_seconds": 64.49,
      "duration_seconds": 11.43,
      "text": "I'd call it mild i notice it more with stress and caffeine there's sweaty palms as well about sweaty palms, I'd call it moderate"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.49,
      "end_seconds": 71.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Okay, what about butterflies in your stomach, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.64,
      "end_seconds": 75.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Yes, for about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 76.32,
      "end_seconds": 86.36,
      "duration_seconds": 10.04,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pulse is 83 beats a minute, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, temp 36.5 degrees. BP is 108 over 70."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.07,
      "end_seconds": 91.01,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "Right, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.97,
      "end_seconds": 96.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "let's move on to the the examination"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.89,
      "end_seconds": 99.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.42,
      "end_seconds": 113.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "there is a fine, fast tremor that goes away when the hands are resting"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.49,
      "end_seconds": 124.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "You can sit up now. Alright, any fainting, palpitations or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.78,
      "end_seconds": 131.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "No, no fainting, palpitations or weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.83,
      "end_seconds": 135.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Has there been any weakness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.17,
      "end_seconds": 139.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "I haven't noticed any weakness"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.18,
      "end_seconds": 143.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "so, is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.48,
      "end_seconds": 147.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "no, my breathing's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.54,
      "end_seconds": 161.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "have you retired yet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.93,
      "end_seconds": 167.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.77,
      "end_seconds": 171.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.07,
      "end_seconds": 175.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.86,
      "end_seconds": 182.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.54,
      "end_seconds": 187.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.91,
      "end_seconds": 193.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.79,
      "end_seconds": 199.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Alendronate, 70 milligrams, maybe, once a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.89,
      "end_seconds": 205.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.54,
      "end_seconds": 213.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "No, it's at home. I was on Thyronorm before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.19,
      "end_seconds": 235.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.2,
      "end_seconds": 243.21,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "I've had an underactive thyroid, yes. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.02,
      "end_seconds": 245.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Okay, any other things?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.74,
      "end_seconds": 249.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Thin bones, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.93,
      "end_seconds": 256.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "yes, thin bones is known to us, good to have that clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.43,
      "end_seconds": 274.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.23,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? My working impression is an anxiety or caffeine-related tremor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.56,
      "end_seconds": 278.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.31,
      "end_seconds": 314.3,
      "duration_seconds": 33.99,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with an anxiety or caffeine-related tremor do well once it's treated properly. I think a thyroid test makes sense here, for tremor. Cut down caffeine and try slow breathing when it starts. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.01,
      "end_seconds": 327.49,
      "duration_seconds": 12.48,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently. I'd like you back in four weeks. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.52,
      "end_seconds": 330.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.42,
      "end_seconds": 333.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "look after yourself"
    }
  ]
}